# Coverage-gate thresholds (ADR-0023). Single source of truth, consumed by the
# CI `integration` job's coverage gate and by `make cover`.
#
# Policy: RATCHET at measured-current — never decrease, target 85%. Raising a
# floor is a deliberate PR that edits this file. A build FAILS below its floor.
#
# Baselines measured 2026-08-27 (module-wide, `-coverpkg=./...`, complete suite):
#   backend  62.3% statements
#   frontend 26.9% lines / 26.8% statements / 17.5% functions / 21.3% branches
# Floors are set a few points under the baseline so CI is deterministically green
# today while still blocking a real regression; ratchet them upward as coverage
# improves.

# Backend Go floor (% statements of the merged/complete `go test -tags=integration
# -coverpkg=./... ./...` profile). Enforced in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
COVERAGE_MIN_BACKEND=60

# Frontend floor (% lines). ENFORCEMENT for the frontend lives in
# frontend/vitest.config.ts `coverage.thresholds` (per-metric: lines/statements/
# functions/branches) — this value documents the headline lines floor and must be
# kept in sync with that config.
COVERAGE_MIN_FRONTEND=25
